---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Free Online Eye Test & Visual Acuity Exam | Snellen & Astigmatism Chart';
const description = 'Check your vision online with our free optometric eye exam. Features calibrated Snellen Tumbling E chart, astigmatism fan dial, and duochrome red-green test. 100% private & instant results.';
const canonicalUrl = 'https://freeiqexam.com/eye-test';

const alternates = {
  // de: '/de/sehtest-online',
  // ru: '/ru/proverka-zreniya-online',
  // pt: '/pt/teste-de-visao-online',
  // fr: '/fr/test-de-vue-en-ligne',
  // es: '/es/test-de-vista-online',
  // id: '/id/tes-mata-online',
  // pl: '/pl/badanie-wzroku-online',
};

const faqItems = [
  [
    'How accurate is an online eye test compared with an optometrist?',
    'An online test can give a useful indication of how well you are seeing at a given distance, but it cannot measure refraction, eye pressure, retinal health, or binocular coordination. Screen size, pixel density, viewing distance, room lighting, and browser zoom all introduce error. Treat the result as a reason to book an examination, never as a replacement for one.'
  ],
  [
    'Why does the test ask me to measure a credit card against the screen?',
    'Visual acuity is defined by the visual angle an optotype subtends at your eye, not by its size in pixels. A 20/20 letter at one metre is 1.45 mm tall regardless of your monitor. Because a browser cannot reliably detect your screen\'s physical pixel density, matching a standard ISO/IEC 7810 ID-1 card (85.60 mm wide) lets the test compute your exact pixels-per-millimetre ratio so optotypes are rendered at true scale.'
  ],
  [
    'Why does the test sometimes refuse to measure sharper than 20/40?',
    'At one metre a 20/20 optotype is 1.45 mm tall, which is roughly 5 pixels on a typical 96 DPI display — too small to draw a five-stroke letter faithfully. Rather than enlarge the letter and report a result it did not actually measure, the test states the sharpest tier your screen can genuinely render. Moving further back and selecting a longer distance makes sharper tiers physically larger and therefore measurable.'
  ],
  [
    'What is the tumbling E and why use it instead of letters?',
    'The tumbling E is a Snellen E rotated to point up, down, left, or right. The viewer reports the direction rather than naming a letter, which removes literacy, language, and letter-recognition ability from the measurement. It is the standard acuity optotype for pre-literate children and for anyone who cannot read the Latin alphabet.'
  ],
  [
    'What does the astigmatism dial actually detect?',
    'A clock dial presents radiating lines in every meridian. When the cornea or lens has an uncorrected cylindrical error, light in one meridian focuses differently from the perpendicular one, so some lines appear darker or sharper than others. If you report a subset of lines as more distinct, that asymmetry is consistent with astigmatism and is worth having measured properly.'
  ],
  [
    'Why do the red and green panels indicate short- or long-sightedness?',
    'This is longitudinal chromatic aberration. Green light around 535 nm refracts more strongly than red around 650 nm, so green focuses slightly in front of the retina and red slightly behind. If red looks sharper, the eye is relatively myopic; if green looks sharper, relatively hyperopic. When both look identical, spherical focus sits close to the retina.'
  ],
  [
    'Can this test tell me my glasses prescription?',
    'No. A prescription specifies sphere, cylinder, axis, and often a reading addition, plus pupillary distance and prism where relevant. This test estimates acuity at one distance and gives a coarse indication of astigmatic asymmetry and spherical balance. Only a licensed optometrist or ophthalmologist can issue a prescription.'
  ],
  [
    'When should I see an optometrist regardless of my score?',
    'Book an examination if you notice a sudden or gradual change in vision, flashes or a shower of floaters, a curtain or shadow across your field, eye pain, persistent redness, double vision, new headaches with visual change, or if you have diabetes, glaucoma, or a family history of eye disease. Sudden vision loss is an emergency — seek care immediately rather than testing online.'
  ]
];

const schemas = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'MedicalWebPage',
    '@id': `${canonicalUrl}#medical-page`,
    name: 'Online Visual Acuity, Astigmatism and Duochrome Screener',
    url: canonicalUrl,
    medicalAudience: 'Patient',
    aspect: 'Diagnostic',
    isAccessibleForFree: true,
    about: {
      '@type': 'MedicalCondition',
      name: 'Refractive Error',
      alternateName: ['Myopia', 'Hyperopia', 'Astigmatism', 'Presbyopia']
    },
    lastReviewed: '2026-09-15'
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebApplication',
    '@id': `${canonicalUrl}#application`,
    name: 'Free Online Eye Test — Snellen, Astigmatism Dial and Duochrome',
    url: canonicalUrl,
    applicationCategory: 'HealthApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Any',
    isAccessibleForFree: true,
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
    accessibilitySummary: 'Keyboard-operable direction responses, on-screen directional controls, full-card calibration slider, visible focus states, live announcements, and a printable screening summary.'
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    '@id': `${canonicalUrl}#breadcrumb`,
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://freeiqexam.com/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Assessments', item: 'https://freeiqexam.com/test' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Eye Test', item: canonicalUrl }
    ]
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    '@id': `${canonicalUrl}#faq`,
    mainEntity: faqItems.map(([name, text]) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text }
    }))
  }
];

const stages = [
  ['intro-section', '1 · Overview'],
  ['calibration-section', '2 · Calibration'],
  ['acuity-section', '3 · Acuity'],
  ['astigmatism-section', '4 · Astigmatism'],
  ['duochrome-section', '5 · Duochrome'],
  ['results-section', '6 · Results']
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl} alternates={alternates} schema={schemas}>
  <Header />

  <main id="assessment-page-content" class="flex-1 bg-white text-zinc-950 dark:bg-black dark:text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 sm:py-14 lg:px-8 lg:py-20">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-zinc-950 dark:hover:text-white">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <a href="/test" class="hover:text-zinc-950 dark:hover:text-white">Assessments</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span aria-current="page" class="text-zinc-950 dark:text-white">Eye Test</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700 dark:border-emerald-900/60 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 dark:text-emerald-300 sm:text-sm">
          Screen-calibrated · Optometric screening
        </div>
        <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl">Free Online Eye Test</h1>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 sm:text-lg">
          Measure visual acuity with a physically calibrated Snellen Tumbling E chart, map meridional blur with an astigmatism clock dial, and check spherical balance on a red-green duochrome. Entirely in your browser — nothing you enter leaves your device.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3 text-sm sm:text-base">
          {['Card-calibrated scale', 'Tumbling E acuity', 'Astigmatism dial', 'Duochrome balance', 'No account required'].map((item) => (
            <span class="rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-4 py-2.5 text-zinc-700 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-300">{item}</span>
          ))}
        </div>
      </header>

      <section id="eye-app" class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-4xl">
        <ol class="stage-strip" aria-label="Test progress">
          {stages.map(([id, label]) => (
            <li data-stage={id} class="stage-chip">{label}</li>
          ))}
        </ol>

        <div class="rounded-[2rem] border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50/80 p-5 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-950/70 sm:p-8">

          <section id="intro-section" class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 p-6 dark:border-emerald-900/50 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 sm:p-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300 sm:text-sm">Before you begin</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">A screening tool, not an examination</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 sm:text-lg">
              This test estimates how well you see at a chosen distance. It cannot measure your refraction, eye pressure, visual fields, or retinal health, and it cannot produce a prescription. Screen size, pixel density, viewing distance, and room lighting all affect the result.
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 sm:text-lg">
              <li class="intro-bullet">Have a standard bank card or ID card ready — you will match it against the screen to calibrate physical scale.</li>
              <li class="intro-bullet">You will need to cover one eye at a time. A palm works better than a hand cupped over the eye.</li>
              <li class="intro-bullet">Test in even, moderate lighting. Avoid a bright window directly behind or in front of the screen.</li>
              <li class="intro-bullet">Wear your usual glasses or contact lenses if you are checking how well your current correction works. Remove them only if you want to know your uncorrected acuity.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
              <button id="begin-eye-test" type="button" class="rounded-2xl bg-emerald-600 px-7 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-white transition hover:scale-[1.02] active:scale-[0.99] focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-emerald-500 sm:rounded-full">Start the vision test</button>
              <span class="self-center text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 sm:text-base">Keyboard: ↑ ↓ ← → to answer during acuity</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 px-5 py-4 text-sm text-red-900 dark:border-red-900/50 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-200 sm:text-base">
              <strong>Sudden vision loss, flashes, a curtain across your vision, or eye pain is a medical emergency.</strong> Do not test online — seek immediate care.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section id="calibration-section" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="calibration-title">
            <div class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-zinc-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-950 sm:p-8">
              <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300 sm:text-sm">Step 1 · Physical calibration</p>
              <h2 id="calibration-title" class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Match a real card to the screen</h2>
              <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 sm:text-lg">
                Hold a standard bank, ID, or library card flat against the screen and drag the slider until the white outline below is exactly the same width as the card. This gives the test your screen's true pixels-per-millimetre ratio, which is what makes the optotypes physically accurate.
              </p>

              <div class="calibration-stage">
                <div id="card-preview" class="card-preview" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              </div>

              <label for="card-slider" class="mt-8 block text-base font-semibold">Card width on screen</label>
              <input id="card-slider" type="range" min="100" max="600" step="1" value="260" class="calibration-slider" />
              <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 sm:text-base">
                <span>Card width: <strong id="card-width-label" class="font-mono">260 px</strong></span>
                <span>Screen scale: <strong id="ppm-readout" class="font-mono">—</strong></span>
              </div>

              <div class="mt-8">
                <p class="text-base font-semibold">Test distance</p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 sm:text-base">Sit or stand so your eye is exactly this far from the screen. Further back makes sharper optotypes physically larger — and therefore measurable.</p>
                <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                  {[['near', '40 cm', '16 in · phone'], ['desk', '1 m', '3.3 ft · desktop'], ['room', '2 m', '6.6 ft'], ['hall', '3 m', '10 ft'], ['snellen', '6 m', '20 ft · Snellen standard']].map(([id, label, hint]) => (
                    <button type="button" data-distance={id} class="distance-button">
                      <span class="distance-label">{label}</span>
                      <span class="distance-hint">{hint}</span>
                    </button>
                  ))}
                </div>
              </div>

              <p id="resolution-warning" class="mt-7 rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 px-5 py-4 text-sm text-amber-900 dark:border-amber-900/50 dark:bg-amber-950/30 dark:text-amber-200 sm:text-base"></p>

              <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap">
                <button id="confirm-calibration" type="button" class="rounded-2xl bg-emerald-600 px-7 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-white transition active:scale-[0.99] sm:rounded-full">Calibrated — begin acuity test</button>
                <button id="skip-calibration" type="button" class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-300 px-6 py-4 text-base font-semibold transition active:scale-[0.99] dark:border-zinc-700 sm:rounded-full">Skip to astigmatism &amp; duochrome</button>
              </div>
              <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 sm:text-base">Calibration is only needed for the acuity chart. The dial and duochrome modules work without it.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="acuity-section" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="acuity-title">
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-end sm:justify-between">
              <div>
                <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300 sm:text-sm">Step 2 · Visual acuity</p>
                <h2 id="acuity-title" class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl"><span id="acuity-eye-label">Right eye</span></h2>
              </div>
              <div class="text-left sm:text-right">
                <div id="acuity-eye-progress" class="text-base font-semibold sm:text-lg">Eye 1 of 3</div>
                <div id="acuity-trial-label" class="mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 sm:text-base">—</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-5 h-2 overflow-hidden rounded-full bg-zinc-200 dark:bg-zinc-800"><div id="acuity-progress-fill" class="h-full rounded-full bg-emerald-600 transition-all duration-300" style="width:0%"></div></div>
            <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3">
              <div id="acuity-tier-dots" class="tier-dots" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 sm:text-base">Three correct clears a level · two misses step down a level or end the eye</p>
            </div>

            <article class="mt-8 rounded-[1.75rem] border border-zinc-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-950 sm:p-9">
              <p id="acuity-instruction" class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50/70 px-5 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-emerald-900 dark:border-emerald-900/50 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 dark:text-emerald-200 sm:text-lg">Cover your LEFT eye.</p>
              <p class="mt-6 text-base text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 sm:text-lg">
                Which direction is the E pointing? Current level <strong id="acuity-tier-label" class="font-mono text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">—</strong>
              </p>

              <div id="optotype-mount" class="mt-6"></div>

              <div class="direction-pad mt-8">
                <div></div>
                <button type="button" data-direction="up" class="direction-button" aria-label="E points up">↑</button>
                <div></div>
                <button type="button" data-direction="left" class="direction-button" aria-label="E points left">←</button>
                <div class="direction-center" aria-hidden="true">E</div>
                <button type="button" data-direction="right" class="direction-button" aria-label="E points right">→</button>
                <div></div>
                <button type="button" data-direction="down" class="direction-button" aria-label="E points down">↓</button>
                <div></div>
              </div>

              <p id="acuity-feedback" class="acuity-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
              <p class="mt-6 text-center text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 sm:text-base">
                Three correct at a level clears it. Two wrong ends that eye.
              </p>
            </article>
          </section>

          <section id="astigmatism-section" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="astig-title">
            <div class="rounded-[1.75rem] border border-zinc-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-950 sm:p-9">
              <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300 sm:text-sm">Step 3 · Astigmatism dial</p>
              <h2 id="astig-title" class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Do any lines look darker or sharper?</h2>
              <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 sm:text-lg">
                Stand or sit at your chosen distance. With one eye at a time, look at the centre of the dial and compare the twelve lines. Some people with uncorrected astigmatism see one or two lines as noticeably darker, bolder, or sharper than the rest. Select every line that stands out.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 sm:text-lg">
                Each ray is selectable on its own, including the two opposite rays that lie on the same line through the centre — those two describe one and the same meridian, so if a line looks blurred at both ends, mark both.
              </p>
              <div id="dial-mount" class="dial-stage mt-8"></div>
              <p id="dial-selection-label" class="mt-6 text-base font-semibold text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300 sm:text-lg">No lines selected yet.</p>
              <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap">
                <button id="submit-astigmatism" type="button" class="rounded-2xl bg-emerald-600 px-7 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-white transition active:scale-[0.99] sm:rounded-full">Continue to duochrome</button>
                <button id="dial-none" type="button" aria-pressed="false" class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-300 px-6 py-4 text-base font-semibold transition active:scale-[0.99] dark:border-zinc-700 sm:rounded-full">All lines look equal</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="duochrome-section" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="duo-title">
            <div class="rounded-[1.75rem] border border-zinc-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-950 sm:p-9">
              <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300 sm:text-sm">Step 4 · Red-green duochrome</p>
              <h2 id="duo-title" class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Which ring looks sharper?</h2>
              <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 sm:text-lg">
                Compare the black ring on the red panel with the black ring on the green panel. Judge <strong>sharpness and clarity</strong>, not brightness — the two colours are deliberately different in luminance. Look at both for a few seconds before deciding.
              </p>
              <div class="duochrome-grid mt-8">
                <div class="duochrome-panel duo-red">
                  <div id="duochrome-red" class="duochrome-target"></div>
                  <span class="duochrome-caption">Red · ~650 nm</span>
                </div>
                <div class="duochrome-panel duo-green">
                  <div id="duochrome-green" class="duochrome-target"></div>
                  <span class="duochrome-caption">Green · ~535 nm</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap">
                <button type="button" data-duo="red" class="duo-choice rounded-2xl border-2 border-red-300 bg-red-50 px-6 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-red-900 transition active:scale-[0.99] dark:border-red-900 dark:bg-red-950/40 dark:text-red-200 sm:rounded-full">Red looks sharper</button>
                <button type="button" data-duo="green" class="duo-choice rounded-2xl border-2 border-emerald-300 bg-emerald-50 px-6 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-emerald-900 transition active:scale-[0.99] dark:border-emerald-900 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 dark:text-emerald-200 sm:rounded-full">Green looks sharper</button>
                <button type="button" data-duo="equal" class="duo-choice rounded-2xl border-2 border-zinc-300 bg-zinc-100 px-6 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-zinc-800 transition active:scale-[0.99] dark:border-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-200 sm:rounded-full">Both look the same</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="results-section" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="results-title">
            <div class="rounded-[1.75rem] border border-zinc-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-950 sm:p-9">
              <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 sm:flex-row sm:items-start sm:justify-between">
                <div>
                  <div id="result-badge" class="result-badge neutral">Acuity result recorded</div>
                  <h2 id="results-title" class="mt-5 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Your vision screening summary</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-600 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-300 sm:text-base">Not a diagnosis</div>
              </div>

              <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
                <article class="score-card reveal"><div class="score-label">Right eye</div><div id="acuity-right" class="acuity-fraction">—</div><div id="acuity-right-note" class="score-status">Best level cleared</div></article>
                <article class="score-card reveal"><div class="score-label">Left eye</div><div id="acuity-left" class="acuity-fraction">—</div><div id="acuity-left-note" class="score-status">Best level cleared</div></article>
                <article class="score-card reveal"><div class="score-label">Both eyes</div><div id="acuity-both" class="acuity-fraction">—</div><div id="acuity-both-note" class="score-status">Best level cleared</div></article>
              </div>

              <p id="acuity-summary-note" class="reveal mt-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 sm:text-lg"></p>

              <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
                <article class="stat-card reveal"><span>Astigmatism dial</span><strong id="astig-result">Not recorded</strong><p id="astig-note" class="stat-note"></p></article>
                <article class="stat-card reveal"><span>Duochrome balance</span><strong id="duo-result">Not recorded</strong><p id="duo-note" class="stat-note"></p></article>
              </div>

              <article class="reveal mt-6 rounded-3xl border border-zinc-200 p-6 dark:border-zinc-800">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 sm:text-base">Test conditions</p>
                <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold sm:text-2xl">What this measurement assumed</h3>
                <p id="calibration-summary" class="mt-4 font-mono text-base sm:text-lg">—</p>
                <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 sm:text-lg">
                  Acuity figures are only as good as the calibration and distance they were measured at. If the card match was approximate, or you sat nearer or further than the selected distance, the true value will differ from the one reported here.
                </p>
              </article>

              <div class="reveal mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap">
                <button id="print-result" type="button" class="rounded-2xl bg-zinc-950 px-7 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-white transition active:scale-[0.99] dark:bg-white dark:text-zinc-950 sm:rounded-full">Print clinician summary</button>
                <button id="share-result" type="button" class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-300 px-6 py-4 text-base font-semibold transition active:scale-[0.99] dark:border-zinc-700 sm:rounded-full">Share summary</button>
